   "d": "2021-11-02",
   "doc": "Q3 R",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "On average, based on bp's current forecasts, at around $60 per barrel Brent and subject to the board's discretion each quarter, bp continues to expect to be able to deliver buybacks of around $1.0 billion per quarter and have capacity for an annual increase in the dividend per ordinary share of around 4% through 2025.",
   "file": "20211102_BP_3Q21-SEA-Part-1-of-1.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-02-08",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "On average, based on bp's current forecasts, at around $60 per barrel Brent and subject to the board's discretion each quarter, bp expects to be able to deliver share buybacks of around $4.0 billion per annum and have capacity for an annual increase in the dividend per ordinary share of around 4% through 2025.",
   "file": "20220208_BP_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-02-08",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "The strong progress bp has made over the past few years has reinforced its confidence in the delivery of its earnings and returns targets for 2025.",
   "file": "20220208_BP_bp-update-on-strategic-progress.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-05-03",
   "doc": "Q1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "bp received divestment and other proceeds of $1.2 billion in the first quarter and continues to expect to receive total proceeds of $2-3 billion during 2022.",
   "file": "20220503_BP_1Q22-SEA-Part-1-of-1.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-08-02",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "The underlying ETR* for 2022 is now expected to be around 35% but is sensitive to the impact that volatility in the current price environment may have on the geographical mix of the group’s profits and losses.",
   "file": "20220802_BP_Release-of-a-capital-market-information.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-02-07",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "As a result of both factors, bp is now targeting group EBITDA of $46-49 billion in 2025 and is aiming for $51-56 billion in 2030, in a $70/barrel (2021 real) oil price environment.",
   "file": "20230207_BP_bp-Integrated-Energy-Company-strategy-update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-04-09",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Also refer to bp's fourth quarter and full year 2023 group results announcement on 6 February 2024 for guidance items which continue to apply unless explicitly stated.",
   "file": "20240409_BP_1Q24-Trading-statement-part-1-of-1.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-05-07",
